# m1 macro processor

The m1 macro processor, originally by Jon Bentley.
Bentley is also the author of Programming Pearls
and many other books about programming.

The m1 macro processor appears in 
Sed & Awk, 2nd Edition
by Dougherty and Robbins.

Bentley also wrote 
[an article about m1](https://www.drdobbs.com/open-source/m1-a-mini-macro-processor/200001791)
that appears in Dr. Dobb's.

I have enhanced my version of m1 with the suggested `@longdefine` and `@undefine` macros,
and a `@calc` macro that incorporates functionality from my Awk-based emulation of dc.
